content.text:
Now let me check what padding the `.ways-sec` section has in the Webflow HTML — just `padding-left/right`, no top/bottom in the CSS. That means the vertical rhythm comes from margin/padding of child elements. The audit says 1440 is 64px short and 375 is 72px taller. These are section-level discrepancies — let me check if there's a missing top/bottom padding on `.ways-sec`:

The Webflow CSS for `.ways-sec` only sets `padding-left: 5%; padding-right: 5%` — no top/bottom padding. The comparison section relies on surrounding margins. The drift is likely from the grid gap, child padding discrepancies, or missing `display: grid` on `waysGrid`. Let me check:

The Webflow `ways-grid` at line 17235:
```css
.ways-grid {
  grid-column-gap: 24px;
  grid-row-gap: 24px;
  grid-template-rows: auto;
}
```
It has NO `display: grid` and NO `grid-template-columns`! The module currently has `display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr`. This is correct because `.ways-grid` is normally combined with Webflow's base grid classes which set `display:grid`. Let me check the Webflow HTML:

